Not every missing event has equal importance. Here is how I would prioritize it against the forensic questions.
Telemetry	Priority	Reason
Successful memfd_create and returned FD	Critical	Currently we cannot identify the created object
FD-to-file-object correlation	Critical	Required for reliable memfd provenance
execveat and execution-object correlation	Critical	Required to investigate FD-based execution
FD duplication and inheritance	High	Required to preserve references across processes
write / pwrite	High	Establishes whether a memfd received data
FD close and object lifetime	High	Prevents false conclusions about object disappearance
Open-file tracking for unlinked files	High	Helps establish whether an unlinked object remains accessible
openat / openat2	High	Establishes access to ordinary filesystem objects
sys_exit_connect	Medium	Distinguishes attempts from successful connection results
mmap	Medium	Adds evidence about file-backed memory usage
ftruncate	Medium	Adds context about memfd/file size manipulation
